## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Thứ Ba: Giải thích khái niệm

### 16:30–16:40 · Shadowing

### 16:40–16:55 · Nói to có ghi âm

**Chủ đề: bạn thiết kế một tính năng AI như thế nào.**

> *"The feature is natural language meal entry — you type what you ate and it fills in the nutrition breakdown.*
> *Three design decisions shaped it. First, the key stays on the server. The app calls my own Edge Function, which authenticates the user, applies a rate limit, and then calls the model. I verified the key isn't in the bundle by unzipping the APK and grepping for it.*
> *Second, structured output rather than free text. I define a Zod schema and the model has to fill it, so I get typed data instead of a paragraph I'd have to parse. The schema includes a confidence field, so the model tells me when it's guessing at a portion size, and the UI flags those differently.*
> *Third — and I think this is the one people skip — nothing is saved automatically. The parse produces a preview the user can edit before confirming. The model is guessing at portions; the user actually knows. And it means the feature degrades gracefully: if the model fails, they just fill the form in manually, which is exactly what they did before.*
> *On cost, I benchmarked a smaller and a larger model on twenty Vietnamese meal descriptions. The larger one was marginally better on ambiguous cases and about fifteen times the price. Since everything goes through a confirmation step anyway, that extra accuracy doesn't change the outcome."*

### 16:55–17:00 · 5 từ mới

| Từ / cụm | Nghĩa | Câu mẫu |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `degrade gracefully` | hỏng có kiểm soát | *The feature degrades gracefully.* |
| `flag` (v) | đánh dấu để chú ý | *The UI flags those differently.* |
| `benchmark` (v) | đo so sánh | *I benchmarked both models.* |
| `marginally` (adv) | nhỉnh hơn không đáng kể | *Marginally better on ambiguous cases.* |
| `shape` (v) | định hình | *Three decisions shaped it.* |

